From: System Electronics
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] medialib: do not require CUSTOM_RHS1 in SDR

IspManager::set_v4l2_controls() sets the sensor WDR mode, then the custom
short exposure readout timing (CUSTOM_RHS1), then the CSI and MCM modes of the
ISP, and gives up at the first control that fails.

CUSTOM_RHS1 belongs to DOL HDR and only exists in the drivers of sensors that
support it. The IMX334 driver does not have it, so with that sensor the call
fails with EINVAL ("bad ctrl: custom_rhs1"), set_config() returns false, and
hailofrontendbinsrc leaves before it hands its configuration to the denoise
element. The first caps event then dereferences the missing configuration in
gst_hailo_denoise_create_srcpad_caps() and the pipeline crashes with SIGSEGV.

In SDR there is no short exposure to time: a failure there is now a warning,
and the CSI and MCM modes are still set. In HDR it stays an error. Sensors
that have the control set it exactly as before.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/hailo-media-library/media_library/src/isp/isp_manager.cpp
+++ b/hailo-media-library/media_library/src/isp/isp_manager.cpp
@@ -241,9 +241,16 @@
         LOGGER__MODULE__ERROR(MODULE_NAME, "Failed to set IMX_WDR");
         return false;
     }
+    // The short exposure readout timing only exists for sensors that support
+    // DOL HDR. In SDR a sensor without the control (IMX334) has nothing to set:
+    // going on keeps the CSI and MCM modes below from being skipped.
     if (!set_custom_rhs1_from_profile())
     {
-        return false;
+        if (desc.is_hdr)
+        {
+            return false;
+        }
+        LOGGER__MODULE__WARNING(MODULE_NAME, "CUSTOM_RHS1 not set, not needed in SDR");
     }
     if (!m_v4l2_ctrl_manager.ext_ctrl_set(get_csi_ctrl_type(), csi_mode))
     {
